          "romaji": "",
          "meaning": "I have to do my homework by tomorrow."
        },
        {
          "japanese": "お<ruby>皿<rt>さら</rt></ruby>、<ruby>洗<rt>あら</rt></ruby>わなきゃいけないね。",
          "romaji": "",
          "meaning": "We need to wash the dishes."
        },
        {
          "japanese": "ごみを<ruby>捨<rt>す</rt></ruby>てなくちゃ。",
          "romaji": "",
          "meaning": "I need to take the rubbish out."
        }
      ],
      "notes": [
        "Used with friends and family, not in formal situations."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Mustn't and may (casual): 〜ちゃだめ / 〜ていい",
      "pattern": "V-ちゃ(じゃ) だめ / V-て いい",
      "explanation": "Casual versions of てはいけない and てもいい.",
      "examples": [
        {
          "japanese": "ここで<ruby>遊<rt>あそ</rt></ruby>んじゃだめ。",
          "romaji": "",
          "meaning": "You can't play here."
        },
        {
          "japanese": "その<ruby>窓<rt>まど</rt></ruby>、<ruby>開<rt>あ</rt></ruby>けちゃだめだよ。",
          "romaji": "",
          "meaning": "Don't open that window."
        },
        {
          "japanese": "これ、<ruby>食<rt>た</rt></ruby>べていい？",
          "romaji": "",
          "meaning": "Can I eat this?"
        },
        {
          "japanese": "ドア、<ruby>閉<rt>し</rt></ruby>めていい？",
          "romaji": "",
          "meaning": "Is it OK if I close the door?"
        }
